<p>I figured it would do well to post an explanation of this SCP for anyone who's having trouble getting it, past/present/future.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">SPOILERS</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">This&nbsp;is&nbsp;copy+pasted&nbsp;from&nbsp;a&nbsp;chat&nbsp;so&nbsp;it&nbsp;could&nbsp;be&nbsp;formatted&nbsp;better.</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>it's some deity/superhuman force/entity/thing that took its original form on earth as a program that described images and provided judgments</p>
<p>the article was written by people affected by the program to be a decoy, so it understates the nature of the anomaly drastically while exposing the reader to the ultimate 'squeeze play' judgment</p>
<ul>
<li>the first judgment implies that the 'inaccuracies' are not actually inaccurate, and that there's reasoning behind the judgments</li>
<li>second one states that, at least in their view, it's the photos themselves that are inaccurate, and 2926 describes what they should be</li>
<li>third one can find out what people agree to be the nature of images fed into 2926, and modify them to match what 2926 thinks they should be</li>
<li>fourth one compels people to basically arrange a situation (you reading the article) where the right person views the 'squeeze play' judgment</li>
<li>fifth one coordinates all of the above to create a consensus reality (what people agree to be real) in which 2926 is capable of manifesting as &quot;the sphinx&quot;</li>
<li>sixth one creates attendants to the sphinx, and this is where it shifts into present tense because they're gonna do this in just a second once you become the sphinx</li>
<li>seventh one states that the sphinx is realized via you, because you have no inaccuracies, and 'the situation is immanent' which i guess means that you were the anomaly, or something like that</li>
</ul>
</div>
